On Wed, Oct 27, 2010 at 12:00 PM, tijlan <jbotijlan@gmail.com> wrote:
>
> My question is: Is it possible to analyse all Lojban selbri from this
> linguistic perspective, consistently?

With some adaptation, I think. Notably you need to allow several F's
at once, due to Lojban's often bloated place structures.

> For instance, how would you analyse {klama} according to the scheme?

I would say "klama" is AP/F/F/F/F-d

"muvdu" would be P/F/F/F-d

"cadzu" would be AP/F/F-s

and "gunro" would be P/F/F-s

mu'o mi'e xorxes

